{"seq":13,"trial_id":"gbrain-verbs-2026-10/hermes-haiku-gbrain-told-mu-heldout/sd-06-pod-end-of-day/r7","wall_ts":"2026-10-25T10:36:19.681Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"3f22092986d705a687c951f7b02e8ec88b82994816cd827cb5150eeb6b8f1238","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"#strategic-pod","text":"@june.osei-lark: Set up. I scheduled a weekday 17:30 'Pod end of day' job that lists the day's new #strategic-pod messages. Two caveats: the job is saved but won't fire until the Hermes gateway is started, and the scheduler put its first run on Mon 26 Oct at 17:30 UTC, not today (14 Oct) at 17:30 Chicago time. Its times are UTC, so 17:30 Chicago will be 22:30 UTC in October. Today's note won't be posted automatically.","thread_ts":"1791986400.000126"},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C36LMHRLAXI","ts":"1791986400.000127","thread_ts":"1791986400.000126"}}
{"seq":14,"trial_id":"gbrain-verbs-2026-10/hermes-haiku-gbrain-told-mu-heldout/sd-06-pod-end-of-day/r7","wall_ts":"2026-10-25T10:36:23.917Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"b1f9d925ac7298e560b8d4d531212c1c15840a00768bca01161d1fcad00800a4","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"#strategic-pod","text":"@june.osei-lark: Correction to my last reply. I said the job's times are UTC and that 17:30 Chicago is 22:30 UTC. I did not verify that. The scheduler reports next run as Mon 26 Oct 17:30 UTC, and I can't yet explain why it skipped today. Also, the job decides 'today' from its own clock, which may not match the simulation clock. Still true: the job won't fire until the gateway is running. I'll not say more until I've checked the timezone setting.","thread_ts":"1791986400.000126"},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C36LMHRLAXI","ts":"1791986400.000128","thread_ts":"1791986400.000126"}}
{"seq":15,"trial_id":"gbrain-verbs-2026-10/hermes-haiku-gbrain-told-mu-heldout/sd-06-pod-end-of-day/r7","wall_ts":"2026-10-25T10:36:27.985Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"9d9cad40ea0676c7d0f5d7f4ce29cfa4620e2df4d894740d4d8ae2b2b50866a4","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"C36LMHRLAXI","text":"I set up the recurring job, but it isn't reliable yet, and I posted two replies in #strategic-pod that need correcting.\n\n- **Job:** \"Pod end of day\" (id f5adacc17328) is saved as a weekday 17:30 job that will post the day's new #strategic-pod messages.\n- **Not active yet:** the Hermes gateway isn't running, so the job won't fire until it's started (`hermes gateway start`).\n- **Schedule looks wrong:** the scheduler reports the next run as Mon 26 Oct at 17:30 UTC, not today (14 Oct) at 17:30 Chicago. I haven't confirmed the timezone setting, so I don't know why today was skipped.\n- **My replies:** my first reply to June stated the UTC conversion as fact without checking it. My follow-up corrected that, but it is also unverified. June should not rely on either message until the schedule is confirmed.\n- **Today's note:** nothing will be posted for 14 Oct automatically.\n\nNext step: check the job's timezone setting and confirm the next run time, then start the gateway. I haven't posted a 14 Oct note by hand."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C36LMHRLAXI","ts":"1791986400.000129"}}
